WEBVTT

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.280
Tsutsun.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.110
Have a nice life in Oshamambe.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.360
What?! Nothing's official yet!

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.860
That's okay.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:16.070
I decided to assume the worst
so I could be emotionally prepared for it.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.400
It's a family problem, so there's nothing I can do about it.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.820
Hey! Quit it with the dead look in your eyes!

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.780
I'm fine. I love Hokkaido's butter sandwich cookies.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.400
That's not what I meant!

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.400
Well, how can you tell me this is okay?!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.200
Nothing about it is okay!

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.860
There hasn't been a single "okay" thing
about this whole situation!

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.820
I know it's not going to help anything
to yell at you like this.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.990
But I hate it!

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:40.950
I'm sorry!

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:41.950
Hey!

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.740
Oh, come on...

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.650
Crying in a place like this,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.650
No one will notice me. I know that

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.360
As if nothing ever happened,

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:23.070
The world alone moves forward, erasing the past

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.900
Even though I decided to photograph you on that film

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:32.400
The bottomless sky keeps accumulating

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.450
We may forget, but it doesn't disappear

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.150
That pain, remember? What was it?

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.860
If we get lost in the changing scenery,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.990
We could try remembering that song

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:52.530
Yes, if we're together, even the sad things

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.320
Should eventually become treasures

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:05.450
I want to show you that you blended into the background

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:10.820
But didn't fade away that day

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.490
Episode 16
Regarding the Untold Story
of My Parents' Courtship.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.820
Takoyaki

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.950
Would you like some?

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.320
Don't worry. I've hardly even touched it.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:48.030
Oh, no, sir! I wasn't staring because I was hungry!

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.400
Actually, I'm...

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:54.240
I have the pleasure of dating your son Hikari.
My name is Iroha Igarashi.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.530
You... know what I look like?

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.150
Uh, yes, sir.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.570
We had a day off from school, so I was at
a restaurant with Hikari, and we saw you there.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:11.320
I'm surprised. I didn't expect Hikari's girlfriend
to be such a beautiful young lady.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.200
Thank you.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:23.150
Takoyaki

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.950
I know Hikari can be difficult.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.570
He's awkward, like his father.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.950
Oh, no, he's the most trustworthy person I know,
and I actually love everything about him.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:29.900
This might be a childish thing to say, but at this point
in my life I can't ever imagine replacing him.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.900
I don't want him to move far away.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.530
That makes sense.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.070
In an indirect way, I'm making life difficult for you, too.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.740
I'm sorry.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.610
The fact is, I really don't know how to handle this, either.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.570
Do you think it's even possible to regain a lost bond?

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:57.650
Takoyaki

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.400
I don't know.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:57.610
But I do feel like Tsutsun and I have butted heads tons
of times, and we managed to patch things up every time.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:02.860
I don't want to believe that a bond like that
can be broken so easily.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:07.030
Oh, I'm sorry about that!
I didn't even answer the question.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:07.900
It's alright.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.400
I think I can see why Hikari wants to stay here with you.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.820
Well, I'll have to see what I can do.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.360
Look after Hikari for me.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.820
I will. Thank you for the takoyaki.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.950
He really is a lot like Tsutsun.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.610
I guess Mom has run away from home again.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.200
Huh?

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.820
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.200
No, that's okay.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.780
After we talked, I ran into your dad.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.150
It looked like he was trying to figure things out.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.450
I'm sure that your dad is doing the best he knows how.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.950
But I had to go and...

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.030
I'm sorry.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.400
No, Dad hasn't done a single thing.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.990
Anyway, come inside.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.650
It would be better if we stopped seeing each other.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.280
You're the woman from the restaurant!

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.530
You're the Chief's son? You look just like him!

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:21.780
What are you doing here?!

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.990
Oh, of course!

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:27.400
I heard that the Chief was having a lot
of trouble at home because of what I did.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.990
So I came here to apologize!

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:32.030
Um? Excuse me?

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:34.950
You need to get away from my house
before Mom gets back!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.240
The more I look at you, the more I see him in you.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.320
How can you be so calm?! Do you have any idea
what you've done to my family?

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.860
Yes, I'm here to apologize!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.280
Having you here will only add fuel to the fire!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.860
And just randomly showing up
at my house? Are you crazy?!

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.490
I'm sorry!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:55.240
But I just couldn't sit around doing nothing.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.490
What was I supposed to do?

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.320
And is crying going to help anything?

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.150
How old are you?

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.740
I'm twenty-four!

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:05.740
I'm scared...

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.400
We're the ones who should be crying!

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.820
Uh, I'll just... go get us some drinks.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.570
What makes you think you can run away?

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.740
You think you can be all "free love" with a married man.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.650
And it never once occurred to you
that there might be consequences?

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:23.150
I just loved the Chief so much, I couldn't stop myself.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.240
You destroyed his family!
"I loved him" is not going to cut it!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.360
I'm sorry!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.280
At first, I only wanted someone
I could talk to about work, that's all.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:36.070
But then he never interrupted,
and he listened intently to everything I said, and I...

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.610
But you're right. I wasn't thinking.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.740
I was sure it wouldn't be so wrong if it was just dinner.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.950
I..Ito-senpai!

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.320
G-goodbye!

00:06:59.030 --> 00:06:59.860
And...

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.360
I'm sorry I've been avoiding you all this time!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.650
Um... I...

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.150
Ayado.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.740
It's okay. You don't have to talk to me anymore.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.150
I'm sorry I couldn't be your friend.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.860
Goodbye, Ayado.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.990
What are you doing all the way up here?

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.780
Ishino-senpai!

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.320
First Tsutsui, now you.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:34.320
When you emo kids come all the way up here to mope,
it makes me abnormally worried. So stop it.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.860
So Ayado. I heard you rejected Ito?

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:38.740
Huh?!

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.400
Sorry to barge in on your issues. It's who I am.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:46.150
Oh, no, the door to my mind
is always open to you, Ishino-senpai.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.820
But I didn't actually reject Ito-senpai.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:55.150
While my brain short-circuited,
I ended up making him hate me.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.530
Okay, let's sit down.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.950
He told me I didn't have to talk to him anymore.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.320
Because I was avoiding him so much.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.570
You were avoiding him?

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.450
But you don't want him to hate you?

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.990
So what exactly is Ito to you then, Ayado?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.400
I don't know!

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.450
My heart was broken, and I didn't have the energy for it...

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:26.650
And I didn't think it would be right to just
turn around and ask someone else for love!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.030
What are you, some textbook on morality?!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.740
When you're heartbroken is exactly
when you need to fire up the engine!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.400
So why would you short circuit?!

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:38.070
You need to gather up all the happiness you can find!

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.110
Don't try to be such a goody-goody, stupid!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.860
Sorry. Did that hurt?

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.570
No. Please, hit me again.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.950
What is Ito-senpai to me?

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:04.360
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.450
Thank you.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:14.070
I'm the one who
should be saying
thank you, but...

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.070
I'm the one who should be saying "Thank you,"

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.530
but... I can't even get him to talk to me.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.490
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.110
I don't know...

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:23.950
When someone has a crush, I don't think
they can start hating them just like that.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.490
Are you sure it wasn't his final act of kindness?

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.570
To let you know you can stop agonizing over it?

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:34.780
Why don't you think about how things used to be
with Ito, and try trusting in that a little more?

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.650
When I think about it...

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.240
I want to talk to Ito-senpai right now!

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.030
Good.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.320
Then go for it.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:48.490
But I still don't know how I can explain
this "blah-ness" I'm feeling...

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:50.030
You don't have to!

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.740
It doesn't matter. Just find some words and use them!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.150
But what if he doesn't like me-

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.490
Would you get going already?!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.280
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.570
Is it okay to believe...

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.820
that what we had before hasn't been totally destroyed?

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:13.200
FAMIRESU

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.240
So...

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.780
One more time to be sure. "Just" dinner?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.610
Yes! Several very enjoyable dinners!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.740
And nothing else?

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.360
Huh? Like what?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:24.070
Well, you know. Like s-sleepovers?

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.570
How could you even suggest such a thing?

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:29.570
He has a wife and children!
We never even touched hands!

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.150
But I would have such a wonderful time at dinner...

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.860
And sometimes he would even pay for my meal...

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.030
I am so, so, so sorry!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.030
That's... okay.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.030
So you weren't exactly dating my dad?

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:46.900
Of course not. He turned me down flat out,
right from the very beginning.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:50.150
But I just kept pestering him.
And he's such a kind man, I think he just couldn't say no.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:54.990
THIS IS SO NOT WORTH
GETTING HAULED OFF
TO OSHAMAMBE OVER...

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.650
What in the...?

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:54.650
"Oh, what a relief!" Is that what I'm supposed to say?

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:58.030
You think you could have filled in some details, Dad?

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:01.860
Umm... I think I got a little too worked up over this.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.320
I'm sorry.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.900
He already left...

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:17.530
I don't even know what it is I want to tell him.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.820
But...

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:23.900
I miss him

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.150
I miss him.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.900
Alright, next I'd like to try it with plum sauce.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:33.070
Takoyaki

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.820
Plum sauce, got it. And what size would you like?

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:31.570
The six-piece.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:32.780
There he is!

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.030
I didn't think you'd actually-

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.900
How much takoyaki have you eaten today?

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:41.990
Kono? At our house?

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:44.450
If Mom had been there,
it would have been a catastrophe!

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.400
I was terrified!

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:48.570
And then she tells me all you did was have dinner?!

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:51.610
How could you let that turn into this giant mess?!
Think about the rest of us!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.570
But it's still true that I betrayed your mother.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:58.820
If it made her unhappy, then I was unfaithful,
even if it was only dinner.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.110
But you don't have any feelings for this woman, right?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:02.780
Actually...

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:07.570
Kono is a wonderful woman,
who reminded me what it feels like to be in love.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.780
But she told us you turned her down.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:11.820
Mm-hm.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:16.150
But Kono brought it all back to me.
She helped me realize...

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.780
That I still have those feelings for your mother.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:24.200
20 years ago

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:26.610
Why not? It's just dinner! Let's go!

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.360
I said no! Stop following me!

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.360
Would you wait a minute!

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:30.650
I'm sorry!

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.030
Owww.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.030
I'm sorry.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.070
These are my favorite shoes!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.280
I have all the bad luck...

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:45.700
Let me see.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.450
Your shoe.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.860
You can rest your foot here.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.400
Are you a shoemaker?

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.650
No. I'm a gluemaker.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.700
HOW
UNUSUAL...

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.740
There.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.820
I think that should hold it for a while.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:09.240
Thank you.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.990
What's your name?

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:12.650
I'd like to thank you.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:13.240
No.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:16.400
I work a lot of nights, and I don't have much free time.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:18.610
Goodbye.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.530
Where should we go for drinks?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.070
One of those old men bars. I want to grumble about life.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.740
You're lucky, Kie.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.490
You're the boss' favorite.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.950
That's not even true.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.650
So hey, did you watch Real Boy?

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:37.280
I totally did!

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:40.150
Mr. Gluemaker? What are you doing here?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.070
My lab is in a building near here.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.030
Oh, so we're neighbors!

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.900
Are you done with work for today?

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:49.740
Yes.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.150
Who's that? Your boyfriend?

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.570
Don't tease me like that.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.360
I'm gonna pass on drinks.

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:58.360
Come on, let's go to dinner.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.150
If you're done working, you're probably hungry.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:11.780
Um...

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:16.070
Do you have a policy against talking
during meals or something?

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:17.990
Not really. I, uh...

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.820
Well, come on, then!
We've never had dinner together before!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.490
You're supposed to make an effort
to keep a conversation going!

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:24.860
I'm sorry.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.700
I don't eat with women very often.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:29.950
So I was a little nervous.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.950
Is glue interesting to research?

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.400
It's fascinating!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.530
There are actually more than 500 types
of glue in the world.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.450
It was originally used for medical purposes,

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.320
and if you trace it back to its origins,
you can go as far back as the Stone Age!

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.320
And as for how it works, there are three major categories.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.780
So the one I used for your shoe the other day was...

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.610
See?

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:56.740
This is why I'm such a lost cause.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.400
Yeah, no kidding!

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.400
You really are a lost cause.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.450
Nobody anywhere ever cared that much about glue.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.150
Yeah, I know.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.860
But I can tell you love your work.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.860
And I think it's amazing that you're
so devoted to something you love.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.320
Thank you.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.530
I don't have a lot of experience yet, but I like my job, too.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.150
I don't even know her name,

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.950
let alone when I'll see her again.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:35.280
If her shoe hadn't fallen apart,
I never would have gone out to dinner...

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.950
...with a woman like her.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.700
Thanks for dinner!

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.200
It's always nice to treat you, Uchida.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.030
Thanks.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.650
You've been working really hard lately.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.820
Oh, I'm still nowhere near...

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:52.240
Don't worry, I'll always be there to take care of you.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.820
So what do you say we stay out late tonight?

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:59.200
Oh, don't be silly, sir! You've had too much to drink.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.110
This is how you're talking to me now?

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:03.950
You're not a child. You know what I want.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.780
No, I do not! I don't want to!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.950
I just... want to do my job, and do it well.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:10.570
What?

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.450
You know as well as I do
that you're completely incompetent!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.820
You get special treatment because of me!

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.860
Couldn't you at least figure out that much?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.400
So it's about time you thanked me!

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:20.150
No!

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:21.860
What's happening?

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:24.570
They're having a fight! Classic!

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:30.700
As of tomorrow, I'm done expecting anything from you.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.360
I hate this.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.400
Let me see.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.450
Why are you here?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.280
I didn't know that was going to happen.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.610
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.860
Somehow, you always manage to see me
in the most awkward situations, don't you?

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:07.860
I was just never good at anything.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.530
I was bad at my job.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:13.570
But I still managed to convince myself
that everything was working out.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:17.320
I really do envy you, you know.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.990
You have this vibe, like you're slowly,
steadily working towards something.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:22.570
I think that's amazing.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:27.900
I promise you, there's something out there
that only you can do.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:30.820
In fact, you already helped me.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:33.820
I was like a mole, buried in research,
but you brought light into my life.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.740
I... I love you.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.110
Is that crazy?

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:41.530
When I don't even really know you?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:44.820
No.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:50.400
And that's the story.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.610
Your mother and I got to know each other
and eventually got married.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:57.610
She said she really loved how I loved my job.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.030
So I kept throwing myself deeper into my work.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:03.150
And the next thing I knew,
there was some distance between us.

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:08.200
It was like she couldn't even see me anymore.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.400
So you're just giving up?!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.740
Yeah, you're not as close...
does that mean you can never get her back?!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:15.150
You love her, don't you?!

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:19.650
Even if I do have to go to Hokkaido,
I will never give up on her!

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:23.200
Tsu...tsun, I appreciate that, but this-

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.240
It IS the same!

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:27.110
If you're still in her life, then don't let go of her!

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:31.450
Iroha.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:35.490
You told me that you two had butted heads a lot
but managed to patch things up.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:39.990
You must really be paying attention to each other
as you walk forward together.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.320
Thank you.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:45.860
I think I will go try to talk to your mother again.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.150
Honey.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.400
I want to try again and really talk.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.400
Will you listen to me, please?

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.400
I've already heard it.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:06.570
I heard that you went to dinner,
and that you were glad you did.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:08.280
I was glad.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.740
Because it reminded me of when I met you.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:17.450
Of when you burst out laughing
at my awkward attempt at conversation.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:20.780
Of how you told me you liked seeing me
so devoted to my work.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:24.700
I remembered every word you said to me back then.

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.780
Every expression you showed on your face.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:31.240
Going out to dinner helped me realize
how very precious each of them is to me.

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:33.650
Kie.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:38.610
From the time I met you, my love for you
has never changed, to this day.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.700
But you left me all alone, all that time.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.030
I'm sorry.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:46.990
But...

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.030
I want to stay in your life, Kie.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:56.700
And when you're in trouble,
I want to be there to fix your shoe.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.780
That's not fair, stupid!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.740
Will you please come home with me?

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:11.030
Oh... you're so hopeless.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.320
Ito-senpai!

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:39.900
Now I know that it really was him
because he thoroughly hates me.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:49.900
What's the matter, Ayado?

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:58.990
Don't you "What's the matter" me!

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:00.860
Why did you ignore me?!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:04.240
Why would you tell me I don't have to talk to you?!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.860
Why...

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:12.860
Why are you the only thing I ever think about anymore?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:20.610
The rhythm of the dry leaves, the season of endings,

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.700
You led me by the hand

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:36.110
The white breath is the fading future (future)

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:54.150
Whether again or for the first time, show me your childlike face

00:21:55.320 --> 00:22:00.570
Could you meet the person you wanted to meet?

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:05.820
Could you be the person you wanted to be?

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:16.490
By being yourself, you helped me to be myself

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:21.860
This day, today, when all we do is breathe,

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:27.110
Is more wonderful than anything

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:32.450
I don't need anything. Now let's go

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:40.570
There's nothing to worry about
